questions.stem:
A lighthouse keeper flashes lamp numbers down to zero with this method:
public static void beacon(int n) { _____; System.out.print(n); beacon(n - 1); }
Which line belongs in the blank?

A grain inspector counts digits recursively, with single digits already handled:
static int digits(int n) { if (n < 10) return 1; return _____; }
Which expression belongs in the blank?

A stair crew totals steps with this method, but stairs(3) returns 7 instead of 6:
public static int stairs(int n) { if (n == 0) return 1; return n + stairs(n - 1); }
What is the fault?

A feed store sums bins lo through hi with this helper:
static int sumRange(int[] a, int lo, int hi) { if (lo > hi) return 0; return _____; }
Which expression belongs in the blank?

A receipt adder overflows the stack with this method:
static int total(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return n + total(n); }
What is the fault?

A signal crew spells messages letter by letter, in order, with this helper:
static void spell(String s) { if (s.isEmpty()) return; _____; }
Which line belongs in the blank?

A swim club totals warm-up laps with this method:
static int sumDown(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return _____; }
Which expression belongs in the blank?

A crate crew undercounts every load with this pair:
public static int sum(int[] a) { return sumRest(a, 1); }
static int sumRest(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length) return 0; return a[i] + sumRest(a, i + 1); }
The first crate never counts. What is the fault?

A wetland monitor counts traded calls with this pair:
static int heron(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return 1 + egret(n - 1); }
static int egret(int n) { if (n <= 0) return 0; return 1 + heron(n - 1); }
Calling heron(3) runs the exchange. What integer is returned?

A badge press prints every order of three distinct letters with this method, one order per line:
static void perm(String done, String rest) { if (rest.isEmpty()) { System.out.println(done); return; } for (int i = 0; i < rest.length(); i++) perm(done + rest.charAt(i), rest.substring(0, i) + rest.substring(i + 1)); }
Calling perm("", "RST") runs the press. How many lines print in total?

A market stall totals morning sales with this helper:
static int sumRest(int[] a, int i) { if (i == a.length) return 0; return a[i] + sumRest(a, i + 1); }
System.out.print(sumRest(new int[]{4, 7, 2}, 0));
What integer is printed?

The market stall audits only its late bins with the same sumRest helper:
System.out.print(sumRest(new int[]{5, 8, 3, 6}, 2));
What integer is printed?

The market stall compares shifts with the same sumRest helper on one till:
int[] till = {4, 7, 2};
System.out.println(sumRest(till, 0) + sumRest(till, 1));
What integer is printed?
